                <pb facs="0319" n="309" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg309"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 610.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 10, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Despatches from the department, numbered
                    from 847 to 851, inclusive, have been received at this legation.</p>
                <p>Under the instructions contained in No. 847, of the 17th of February, I have
                    addressed a note to Lord Russell respecting the conduct of Mr. Butterfield, the
                    British vice-consul at Key West. A copy is transmitted.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHAELES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d128-a1.xml" xpointer="d128-a1"/>
